  "notes": "All 8 GPUs were shared with another user's jobs at 90-100% utilization for the whole session, so ms values are upper bounds. Multinex is slow for 44.6K params: torch.profiler shows aten::native_layer_norm at 72.81% of CUDA time at 400x600 (channels-last LayerNorm in Multinex_arch.py). ms_600x400/ms_1080p: repo basicsr/complexity.py, random input, 10 warm-up + 50 timed runs, CUDA events + torch.cuda.synchronize, fp32, batch 1, cudnn.benchmark on. ms_multinex in 'mine': 10 warm-up + 50 timed, torch.cuda.synchronize + perf_counter, dagger NoRef weights, input padded to a multiple of 32 as test_noref.py does. vram_mb = torch.cuda.max_memory_allocated for one 600x400 forward (pretrained LOL-v1 weights, inference_mode). mean_brightness = mean of all uint8 RGB values (0-255). Visual (from the side-by-side PNGs): Nano shows colour casts (beige on LOL 547, navy on DICM/18, blue/orange blotches on MEF) with blotchy noise in dark areas; Multinex is close to ground truth on LOL but on DICM/18 stays under-exposed with a green cast. test_noref.py printed 'RuntimeWarning: Mean of empty slice' inside NIQE during DICM; all 104 per-image NIQE/BRISQUE values per model are finite, so no image was dropped from the averages. Warnings: FutureWarning for torch.cuda.amp.GradScaler in basicsr/models/image_restoration_model.py (harmless). README self-ensemble example names Multinex_LOLv1.pth / LOL_v1, but the file is Multinex_LOL-v1.pth."
